[9.1,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what ov does in your Azure subscription (location northeurope); --debug shows every command:\r\n\r\n  1. SSH key: the stack's own key pair, its public half handed to the template (.openvidu/azure/ov-e2ep-a111205-key.pub)\r\n  2. Template: render the single node template into .openvidu/azure/cf-openvidu-pro-singlenode.bicep\r\n     and its secure parameters into .openvidu/azure/secure-parameters.json (0600)\r\n  3. Resource group: create ov-e2ep-a111205-rg in northeurope\r\n  4. Machines: Create the deployment ov-e2ep-a111205 with the machine, which installs OpenVidu Pro on itself (about 4 minutes)\r\n  5. Wait for OpenVidu to be up, read what it published (URL, credentials) and register this directory as the stack\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\r\n▶ Create the machines on Azure…\r\n"]
[10.486,"o","   · create the resource group ov-e2ep-a111205-rg in northeurope\r\n"]
[15.124,"o","   · create the machines from .openvidu/azure/cf-openvidu-pro-singlenode.bicep (this returns when Azure is done)\r\n"]
[20.124,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so `ov stack destroy` removes it even if the wait below fails\r\n   ✓ Create the machines on Azure\r\n\r\n▶ Wait for the machines to deploy OpenVidu…\r\n"]
